From 055fc566695dce9963b32ed07d03eb7f88120b73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:17:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion,app): turning kinds approach and rough from the
 setup stock

Profile rough and finish, groove rough and finish, parting, threading and
form now read the revolved stock envelope (the bar's widest radius about
the part's fitted axis, StockEnv), passed in from the app layer the way
the meridian rapid law reads the stock. In a bar wider than the part:

- every approach and retract stands clear of the bar's OD by a 1 mm
  radial clearance (an insert's nose added);
- the profile rough's ladder counts its rungs from the bar's OD down to
  the part plus stock-to-leave, dropping rungs that never reach under
  the OD; groove rough and parting peck down from the OD.

A 20 mm bar roughed to a 12 mm part now generates passes from r 10 down
and posts clean, where #103's law refused it with RapidInStock. A bar
no wider than the part (every lathe golden) keeps the part-based program
unchanged; no readable stock keeps it too and names that in a path note.
Facing (#122), the contour rides and boring are not changed. Parting
moves from blade.rs to parting.rs for the size budget; turning_profile's
fixture moves from a 40 mm box to bar-sized stock.

Fixes #130

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
